==Battleground==
*3 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Dagshund]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**3 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Dagshund]]s spawn, delay 53.33~56.67 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,700f</sup>.
**2 [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] spawn, delay 70~73.33 seconds<sup>2,100f~2,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A high-level [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] with [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] is enough to stall the first enemies. After THE FOLIVOREAN spawns, keep spamming Jamiera Cat along with Eraser Cat and any cat with more than 500 range (e.g. [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Dark Emperor Catdam]], [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] etc.). [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is incredibly helpful against the Wild Doges, Rain Ds and THE FOLIVOREAN alike, especially above level 30.

==Trivia==
*The Strongest Behemoth's Japanese name, Saikyō no Mōjū (最強の猛獣, "The Strongest Fierce Beast"), is also present in the Japanese descriptions of [[THE SLOTH]] and [[THE FOLIVOREAN]]. Although the stage's English name translates it as "Behemoth", 猛獣 ''Mōjū'' ("Fierce Beast") is different from the [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemy type's Japanese name (超獣 ''Chōjū'', "Super-Beast").

